<!--
---
description: "READ 1000 — Women's Sphere (FULL SBA): one of the two parallel forms of the READ 1000 module. Across five parts, a study group (peers Danielle, Joe, Karis; reading instructor Professor Booker) works through three texts — an American Yawp Ch. 11 textbook excerpt on women and the 'cult of domesticity', the 1850 engraving 'The Sphere of Woman', and a magazine article on today's 'tradwife' trend the instructor hands out on paper — building toward PULLING IT TOGETHER, a four-or-five-sentence synthesis, by rating vocabulary, close-reading and highlighting, checking a peer's notes, answering comprehension questions, and analyzing the image, then finally writing four or five sentences comparing the 1800s ideal of womanhood with today's 'tradwife' trend. Tabbed design: a Discussion tab holding the scripted conversation beside the activity pane — the conversation opens each activity into the pane with a target embed, which also leaves a labelled, clickable marker in the transcript at the point the activity happened — then one tab per reading (Professor Hale's lecture, the four American Yawp parts, the engraving). Pulling It Together is the last screen the conversation opens in the pane. Companion to the parallel Temperance form."
category: writing
index: 58
lang: en-Latn-US
---
-->

<!--
  READ 1000 — Women's Sphere — FULL SBA (Part 1)

  The Women's Sphere form. Its tabbed interface, its UseHistory-driven pane, its
  attention cues, and its five-part arc are the ones the parallel form has; what
  differs is the content —

    * Part 3 (Main Readings) — the textbook (American Yawp Ch. 11, "The Cotton
      Revolution": women, the family, and the "cult of domesticity"), read in
      four chunks with vocabulary, a note-check, close reading, and
      comprehension; then the engraving ("The Sphere of Woman," Godey's Lady's
      Book, 1850); then the magazine article ("The Unglamorous Truth About the
      Average Tradwife"), which the instructor hands out ON PAPER (it is not
      carried online). The engraving comes BEFORE the article, since it is
      immediately relevant to the American Yawp text.
    * Part 4 — a cross-text synthesis (sort "then vs. now"; evaluate peer comparisons).
    * Part 5 — PULLING IT TOGETHER, the culminating synthesis (four or five
      sentences comparing the 1800s ideal of womanhood with today's "tradwife"
      trend), and a wrap-up.

  Course-team departures from the storyboard, in both forms:
    * "Joe's notes" (the note-checking matrix) tests the TEXTBOOK.
    * Professor Booker is the READING instructor.

  Layout. The tab strip is the top level, and it is organized around ONE TAB PER
  THING TO GO BACK TO:

    Discussion             the session itself — the scripted conversation on the
                           left, the activity pane (a UseHistory the conversation
                           drives) on the right
    Prof. Hale's Lecture   \
    Textbook 1..4          |  the readings, each on its own tab, so a student can
    The Sphere of Woman    /  reopen any one of them at any point

  Every reading tab is a <Use ref="..."> of the very same block the conversation
  parks in the activity pane, NOT a second copy: one block, one state, two doors.

  The magazine article has no tab — it is a paper handout (see womens_sphere_article_read).

  Activity screens live in womens_sphere_activities.olx. Ids are
  prefixed `womens_sphere_`, the form's name; the parallel form uses
  `temperance_`.

  How the pane is driven. The conversation opens each activity screen with a
  TARGET EMBED in the chatpeg —

      ::womens_sphere_vks [display=target:womens_sphere_pane label="How familiar are these words?"]

  — rather than a bare `womens_sphere_pane <- womens_sphere_vks` set command. The screen still lands
  HERE, in the womens_sphere_pane pane; what the embed adds is a small labelled button left
  behind in the transcript at the point in the discussion where that activity
  happened. Clicking it repoints the pane at that screen again. The repoint
  fires once per screen (CompactPopout persists a `repointed` flag).

  Only `womens_sphere_pane <- womens_sphere_pane_blank` is still a set command — parking the pane empty is
  not an activity, so there is nothing to mark or to return to.
-->

<Tabs id="womens_sphere_module" title="Women's Sphere — Full SBA (READ 1000)" launchable="true">

  <!-- ===== Tab 1 (index 0): the session — conversation + activity pane ===== -->
  <Vertical id="womens_sphere_tab_main" title="Discussion">

    <!-- Attention cues. Students don't notice the right pane changing and don't
         know where to look, so every screen the chat opens gets a pulse (Flash)
         as it lands, and the screens with something to fill in also get the
         caret (FocusAction). Reading screens get the pulse alone.

         These live HERE, outside the SplitPanel, and NOT inside the screens. A
         Trigger mounted inside a UseHistory screen is unmounted the moment the
         pane moves on, so it never observes its own expression go false and
         never re-fires. Mounted out here it stays alive for the whole session,
         so mode="each" means each visit. -->

    <!-- HACK: the DefinitionKey(...) normalization in these watch expressions is
         NOT long-term stable and should NOT be copied into other courses. It papers
         over the arrow-era assumption that pane values are bare screen names; target
         embeds write qualified refs. The intended fix is cues riding the embed itself
         (flash=/focus= on the ::screen [display=target:...] line) so no pane-value
         comparison exists at all — see bugs.md. We ship this and clean up later. -->
    <Trigger id="womens_sphere_intro_cue"      watch="DefinitionKey(@womens_sphere_pane.value) === DefinitionKey('womens_sphere_intro')"      mode="each">
      <Flash id="womens_sphere_intro_flash"      target="womens_sphere_intro" />
    </Trigger>

    <Trigger id="womens_sphere_vks_cue"        watch="DefinitionKey(@womens_sphere_pane.value) === DefinitionKey('womens_sphere_vks')"        mode="each">
      <Flash id="womens_sphere_vks_flash"        target="womens_sphere_vks_grid" />
      <FocusAction id="womens_sphere_vks_focus"  target="womens_sphere_vks_grid" />
    </Trigger>

    <!-- The readings. Each is an Annotate (or, for the engraving, an image);
         the pulse goes on the passage itself, which is the thing to work on. -->

    <!-- Prof. Hale's lecture has no cue: it is an optional reference on its own
         tab now, never parked in the pane, so there is nothing to point at. -->

    <Trigger id="womens_sphere_read_1_cue"       watch="DefinitionKey(@womens_sphere_pane.value) === DefinitionKey('womens_sphere_read_1')"       mode="each">
      <Flash id="womens_sphere_read_1_flash"       target="womens_sphere_read_1_annotate" />
    </Trigger>

    <Trigger id="womens_sphere_read_2_cue"      watch="DefinitionKey(@womens_sphere_pane.value) === DefinitionKey('womens_sphere_read_2')"      mode="each">
      <Flash id="womens_sphere_read_2_flash"      target="womens_sphere_read_2_annotate" />
    </Trigger>

    <Trigger id="womens_sphere_read_3_cue"       watch="DefinitionKey(@womens_sphere_pane.value) === DefinitionKey('womens_sphere_read_3')"       mode="each">
      <Flash id="womens_sphere_read_3_flash"       target="womens_sphere_read_3_annotate" />
    </Trigger>

    <Trigger id="womens_sphere_read_4_cue"       watch="DefinitionKey(@womens_sphere_pane.value) === DefinitionKey('womens_sphere_read_4')"       mode="each">
      <Flash id="womens_sphere_read_4_flash"       target="womens_sphere_read_4_annotate" />
    </Trigger>

    <!-- The article is read on PAPER, so the only thing on screen to point at is
         the instruction block. The caret is deliberately NOT parked on its Done. -->
    <Trigger id="womens_sphere_article_cue"    watch="DefinitionKey(@womens_sphere_pane.value) === DefinitionKey('womens_sphere_article_read')" mode="each">
      <Flash id="womens_sphere_article_flash"    target="womens_sphere_article_read" />
    </Trigger>

    <Trigger id="womens_sphere_image_cue"        watch="DefinitionKey(@womens_sphere_pane.value) === DefinitionKey('womens_sphere_image')" mode="each">
      <Flash id="womens_sphere_image_flash"        target="womens_sphere_image_figure" />
    </Trigger>

    <!-- The tasks. -->

    <Trigger id="womens_sphere_notes_cue"  watch="DefinitionKey(@womens_sphere_pane.value) === DefinitionKey('womens_sphere_notes')"  mode="each">
      <Flash id="womens_sphere_notes_flash"  target="womens_sphere_notes_grid" />
      <FocusAction id="womens_sphere_notes_focus" target="womens_sphere_notes_grid" />
    </Trigger>

    <!-- Highlighting is worked by dragging over the text and matching by
         clicking pairs, so neither task has a single control to park a caret
         on — pulse only. -->
    <Trigger id="womens_sphere_gram_svo_cue" watch="DefinitionKey(@womens_sphere_pane.value) === DefinitionKey('womens_sphere_gram_svo')" mode="each">
      <Flash id="womens_sphere_gram_svo_flash" target="womens_sphere_gram_verb" />
    </Trigger>

    <Trigger id="womens_sphere_gram_np_cue" watch="DefinitionKey(@womens_sphere_pane.value) === DefinitionKey('womens_sphere_gram_np')" mode="each">
      <Flash id="womens_sphere_gram_np_flash" target="womens_sphere_gram_np_match" />
    </Trigger>

    <Trigger id="womens_sphere_gram_structure_cue" watch="DefinitionKey(@womens_sphere_pane.value) === DefinitionKey('womens_sphere_gram_structure')" mode="each">
      <Flash id="womens_sphere_gram_structure_flash" target="womens_sphere_gram_structure" />
    </Trigger>

    <Trigger id="womens_sphere_gram_antecedent_cue" watch="DefinitionKey(@womens_sphere_pane.value) === DefinitionKey('womens_sphere_gram_antecedent')" mode="each">
      <Flash id="womens_sphere_gram_antecedent_flash" target="womens_sphere_gram_antecedent" />
    </Trigger>

    <!-- The comprehension questions are chat-embedded; the pane holds the
         full excerpt to read from, so this is a reading cue — pulse, no caret. -->
    <Trigger id="womens_sphere_comp_reading_cue" watch="DefinitionKey(@womens_sphere_pane.value) === DefinitionKey('womens_sphere_comp_reading')" mode="each">
      <Flash id="womens_sphere_comp_reading_flash" target="womens_sphere_comp_reading" />
    </Trigger>

    <Trigger id="womens_sphere_synth_sort_cue" watch="DefinitionKey(@womens_sphere_pane.value) === DefinitionKey('womens_sphere_synth_sort')" mode="each">
      <Flash id="womens_sphere_synth_sort_flash" target="womens_sphere_synth_sort_grid" />
      <FocusAction id="womens_sphere_synth_sort_focus" target="womens_sphere_synth_sort_grid" />
    </Trigger>

    <Trigger id="womens_sphere_final_cue" watch="DefinitionKey(@womens_sphere_pane.value) === DefinitionKey('womens_sphere_final')" mode="each">
      <Flash id="womens_sphere_final_flash" target="womens_sphere_final_write" />
      <FocusAction id="womens_sphere_final_focus" target="womens_sphere_final_write" />
    </Trigger>

    <Trigger id="womens_sphere_conclusion_cue" watch="DefinitionKey(@womens_sphere_pane.value) === DefinitionKey('womens_sphere_conclusion')" mode="each">
      <Flash id="womens_sphere_conclusion_flash" target="womens_sphere_conclusion_md" />
    </Trigger>

    <SplitPanel id="womens_sphere_split" sizes="40, 60">

      <StartPane>
        <!-- height is a FIXED 460px, not the "flex-1" default. This transcript
             runs long, and with flex-1 there is nothing upstream constraining the
             pane, so the chat grows taller with every message and pushes the
             activity pane off the bottom of the screen. A fixed box scrolls
             internally instead. The attribute has to sit on <Chat>, NOT on
             <StartPane> (SplitPanel drops attributes on the pane tag). -->
        <Chat id="womens_sphere_chat"
              src="womens_sphere_dialogue.chatpeg"
              cast="characters.cast"
              height="460px" />
      </StartPane>

      <EndPane>
        <UseHistory id="womens_sphere_pane" initial="womens_sphere_intro" />
      </EndPane>

    </SplitPanel>
  </Vertical>

  <!-- ===== Tab 2 (index 1): the background lecture ===== -->
  <Vertical id="womens_sphere_tab_lecture" title="Prof. Hale's Lecture">
    <Use ref="womens_sphere_lecture" />
  </Vertical>

  <!-- ===== Tabs 3-6 (indices 2-5): the American Yawp excerpt, one tab per
                 part, in reading order. These are the same four Annotate
                 blocks the conversation walks through. ===== -->

  <Vertical id="womens_sphere_tab_textbook_1" title="Textbook 1: New Roles">
    <Use ref="womens_sphere_read_1" />
  </Vertical>

  <Vertical id="womens_sphere_tab_textbook_2" title="Textbook 2: Cult of Domesticity">
    <Use ref="womens_sphere_read_2" />
  </Vertical>

  <Vertical id="womens_sphere_tab_textbook_3" title="Textbook 3: The True Woman">
    <Use ref="womens_sphere_read_3" />
  </Vertical>

  <Vertical id="womens_sphere_tab_textbook_4" title="Textbook 4: A Public Role">
    <Use ref="womens_sphere_read_4" />
  </Vertical>

  <!-- ===== Tab 7 (index 6): the third text — the 1850 engraving ===== -->
  <Vertical id="womens_sphere_tab_image" title="The Sphere of Woman">
    <Use ref="womens_sphere_image" />
  </Vertical>


</Tabs>
